-- 103: Mountain West fishing rules (US plan step 4): Montana, Idaho, Wyoming, Colorado, Utah, Nevada, Arizona, New Mexico
-- Checked 2026-10-22 in each state's own guide (links in source_url): Montana FWP 2026 Fishing Regulations (district Standard Daily and Possession Limits,
-- Western p. 23, Central p. 49, Eastern p. 79); Idaho Fishing Seasons & Rules 2025-2027 (General Daily Limits for each of the 7 regions);
-- Wyoming 2026 Fishing Regulations brochure (Statewide Creel Limits, p. 3; in effect Jan 1, 2026); Colorado 2026 Fishing brochure (Statewide Bag &
-- Possession Limits, p. 10; season March 1, 2026 – March 31, 2027; the brochure linked from cpw.state.co.us/fishing);
-- Utah 2026 Fishing Guidebook (Daily limits, p. 7); Nevada 2026 fishing guide (NDOW's official guide on eRegulations, linked from ndow.org: Western,
-- Eastern and Southern Region daily limits + general statewide regulations); Arizona 2025 & 2026 Fishing Regulations (amended Jan 30, 2026; statewide
-- daily bag limits, p. 3); New Mexico 2026-2027 Fishing Rules & Info (cold water p. 17, warm water p. 29).
-- A state rule is a normal fish_rules row whose `regions` holds the 2-letter state code. Needs setup/94 first (its check already allows these codes).
-- Where a rule changes by district, region, season or water the app can only show one number, so the STRICTER one is the size / bag and the note has the rest
-- (Montana: the strictest of its 3 districts; Idaho: the strictest of its 7 regions; Nevada: the strictest of its 3 regions).
-- NOT added: steelhead / ocean-run salmon (Idaho and others set them in separate season brochures), Wyoming northern pike (no statewide number, only
-- drainage exceptions), Montana Western District walleye (must be killed and reported; see the note on the walleye row).
-- Insert only; no delete / drop.

insert into fish_rules (species, match, regions, min_in, max_in, measure, one_over, bag, release_only, closed, open_only, note, source_url, verified_on, active) values
